.TH GXWI-PACKAGE-MANAGER 1 "2026-10-06" "Peios"
.SH NAME
gxwi-package-manager \- install, update and remove software, and choose where it comes from, on a GXWI desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gxwi-package-manager
.SH DESCRIPTION
Package Manager is the desktop's window on
.BR peipkg (1).
Open it from the launcher (type package). It takes no arguments. It has no
authority of its own: it runs peipkg as the person, so what they may install
or remove is exactly what they could with the command, and every change is
the same transaction, with the same history and audit record.
.PP
Installed lists every installed package, with its version and where it came
from; one opened shows its details, what it needs and provides, and its
files, with Check Files, Update to and Remove. Available lists what the
repositories offer that isn't installed, with Install, and Install from
File for a .peipkg file, which opens the file dialog. Updates shows the newer
versions waiting, after refreshing the trusted repositories, with Update and
Update All. History lists every change, newest first, with Undo for the most
recent and Resolve for one that was interrupted. Repositories lists each
repository, with Refresh All, Add Repository, Trust and Remove. Roles shows
each claim and what holds it, and moves it to another package. Installation
Roots shows the named roots; they are added with peipkg root.
.PP
Every change goes the same way. First the plan: what will be installed,
updated, moved back or removed, before anything happens. Then each elevated
action on its own, such as a downgrade or a package taking over another's
files, asked with Allow This; the approval is recorded in the audit stream.
Then the plan's own question, then progress, then the outcome, with
anything peipkg warned of. A removal can stop to ask about a configuration
file changed since it was installed. Once the plan is approved, the change
finishes even if the window is closed.
.PP
Some refusals have a way on, offered once: Continue Anyway when a
repository's information is out of date, Replace It when a file that
belongs to no package is in the way, and Update Anyway when the package's
publisher says it is updated another way. Package Manager never confirms a
repository's trust for the person: Trust shows the signing key and runs the
trust ceremony only when they confirm it, and update checks refresh only
repositories already trusted.
.PP
It asks the system what the person may do. If they may not read peipkg's
records, every section says so once and shows nothing more; as shipped,
only Administrators may. If they may read them but not change them,
everything is shown and nothing can be changed, with the reason said once.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/apps/dev.peios.gxwi-package-manager.toml
Its application declaration.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/peipkg
What it runs for every query and change.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/gxwi-file-dialog
The file dialog, which Install from File opens.
.TP
.I /var/state/peipkg/db.sqlite
.TQ
.I /var/state/peipkg/lock
peipkg's database and lock, which it opens, changing nothing, to learn
whether the person may read and change what is installed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR peipkg (1),
.BR gxwi-file-dialog (1).
.PP
Package Manager, at learn.peios.org.
